      "message": "@ffilzlnx@mindspring.com\n\nAck. You are absolutely right that changing it to a pointer (char *) breaks the intended memory layout.\nThe issue is that C++ compilers do not support Flexible Array Members (FAMs).\nSince the .cc files only include the header and do not actually use the structure, the most reliable cross-language workaround is using a one-element array placeholder to satisfy the C++ compiler:\n#ifdef __cplusplus\n\tchar xattr_content[1]; // Placeholder for C++ compatibility\n#else\n\tchar xattr_content[]; // Standard FAM for C compilation\n#endif\n\nthis approach maintains the memory layout required by the C files while providing a valid, near-identical size placeholder for the C++ compiler.",
      "parentUuid": "decf2512_388ef8eb",
